      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Viktor tells the kitchen staff to leave through the back and front doors. But the back door is blocked. An immigration major introduces himself to Viktor. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Попробуй новый вариант блюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, выход через зал закрыт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мы выходим по одному человеку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Половина идёт через зал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что вы за идиоты?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Быстро ко мне в кабинет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Добрый день, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Я майор миграционной службы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Мы можем пройти в кабинет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "К сожалению, я не могу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мне нужно готовить для гостей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Хорошо, я подожду вас здесь.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Попробуй новый вариант блюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Try the new version of the dish.' The first content word means 'to try', and 'of dish' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, выход через зал закрыт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, the exit through the hall is closed.' Notice the word order: 'chef' comes first, and 'is closed' finishes the sentence. Chef Viktor answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мы выходим по одному человеку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We exit one person at a time.' In Russian, 'we' leads into 'person' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Половина идёт через зал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Half goes through the hall.' Chef Viktor starts with 'half' and pairs it with 'goes' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что вы за идиоты?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What kind of idiots are you?' The key word here means 'what', which Chef Viktor combines with 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Быстро ко мне в кабинет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Quickly to my office.' Chef Viktor starts with 'quickly' and pairs it with 'to me' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Добрый день, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good afternoon, Viktor Petrovich.' the speaker puts 'good' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'day'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Я майор миграционной службы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am a major of the migration service.' In Russian, 'I' leads into 'service' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Мы можем пройти в кабинет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Can we go to the office?' The first content word means 'we', and 'office' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "К сожалению, я не могу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Unfortunately, I cannot.' A compact expression built around 'regret' and 'can'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мне нужно готовить для гостей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I need to cook for the guests.' Listen for the word meaning 'to me' right alongside 'necessary' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Хорошо, я подожду вас здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, I will wait for you here.' the speaker uses the polite plural 'you' here alongside 'good', keeping a formal or respectful tone. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
